<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="017" project="spaarke-intake-pipeline-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-11: Approval: team Work Item, claim, one approve/reject endpoint, Decision Record for both, approved SPE version, resume from AwaitingApproval</title>
    <phase>1 Pipeline core and first doors</phase>
    <gate>after:013,010</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Tags bff-api and auth; new endpoint, service and authorization filter.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Auth-sensitive: fail-closed authorization on the endpoint that releases AI output (ADR-003/008/034, NFR-02); idempotent approve.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P1-C</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>file-overlap with 023 and 024 on EndpointMappingExtensions.cs and the intake DI module.</parallel-reason>
    <deps>013, 010</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, endpoints, auth, authorization, dataverse</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Implement intake approval: the Approve stage creates ONE team Work Item (`IActionSeam.CreateTaskAsync`) owned by the request's owning team and parks the run in AwaitingApproval. Add ONE endpoint, `POST /api/intake/runs/{runId:guid}/decision`, body `{ "action": "claim" | "approve" | "reject", "reason"?: string }`: claim sets the assigned attorney; approve writes the Decision Record, captures SPE versions, sets the run Approved and enqueues Return; reject writes the Decision Record, closes the run and returns the request to "In review". Authorization fails closed.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in ASP.NET Core Minimal APIs, endpoint-filter authorization, Dataverse write paths and ADR-004 idempotency. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>An Approve stage creating one Work Item per run, and an endpoint + filter + service implementing claim/approve/reject with the status-code contract below, Decision Records and approved versions recorded for Return; tests for every case.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-11, NFR-01/02/08; owner: team queue then claim; the Console (019) and MDA form (018) both call this one endpoint (ADR-002). Run-state API, Return job type and intake DI module come from 013; request columns from 010.</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Intake/IntakeApprovalEndpoints.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Intake/IntakeApprovalAuthorizationFilter.cs</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/IntakeApprovalService.cs</file>
      <file role="new">tests/integration/contract/Api/Intake/IntakeApprovalEndpointsContractTests.cs (contract) + tests/integration/auth/Intake/IntakeApprovalAuthorizationTests.cs (auth path) + tests/integration/data-mutation/Intake/IntakeApprovalServiceTests.cs (write path)</file>
      <file role="modify">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/EndpointMappingExtensions.cs</file>
      <file role="modify">the intake DI module and Approve-stage hook created by task 013 under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Infrastructure/DI/ and Services/Intake/ (exact names set by 013)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Ai/PublicContracts/IActionSeam.cs (CreateTaskAsync :44, degraded-success contract)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Signals/DecisionRecordWriter.cs (WriteAsync :750; registered SignalsModule.cs:70; used by Services/Signals/GateDecisionRecordJob.cs)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/InvoiceApprovalEndpoints.cs (domain approve endpoint shape: route group, filter, ProblemDetails codes) — read only, do not edit</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Dataverse/RecordOwnershipResolver.cs (IRecordOwnershipResolver.ResolveOwningTeamAsync :112)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Filters/PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs (team-membership check inside an endpoint filter)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="013" status="pending">Orchestrator stage machine, run-state write API, Return job type, intake DI module, kill switch.</dependency>
      <dependency task="010" status="pending">sprk_servicerequest stage, assigned attorney (sprk_assignedtointernal or new column), current run.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="ADR-008">SCOPE = the decision endpoint. Authorization runs in an endpoint filter (`IntakeApprovalAuthorizationFilter`), not in the handler body; the route group also carries `RequireAuthorization()`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-003">SCOPE = the filter. Allowed caller = a member of the team owning the run's `sprk_servicerequest` (user owner → `IRecordOwnershipResolver.ResolveOwningTeamAsync`). Read fault or unresolved team → 403, nothing written (fail closed). Never trust ids from the body.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-034">SCOPE = the membership check. Use the existing team-membership read used by `PlaybookAuthorizationFilter.cs`; do not add a second membership mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002">SCOPE = request stage, current run, assigned attorney. Only this endpoint/service and the 013 orchestrator write them; clients only call the endpoint. No plugin.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004">SCOPE = approve and the Approve stage. Replay-safe: deterministic Decision Record id per (runId, decision); create-once Work Item marker; Return enqueued with key `intake-return:{runId}`; atomic claim, never `IIdempotencyService` check-then-set alone.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007">SCOPE = approved-version capture. Read the current SPE version id of each output `sprk_document` through `SpeFileStore` only.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">SCOPE = every non-200 response. ProblemDetails with a stable `errorCode` (INTAKE_RUN_NOT_FOUND, INTAKE_FORBIDDEN, INTAKE_RUN_WRONG_STATE, INTAKE_INVALID_ACTION, INTAKE_DISABLED) and the correlation id; no document or request text.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-032">SCOPE = the endpoint. When the intake kill switch from 013 is off, the endpoint returns 503 INTAKE_DISABLED (Null-Object), and nothing is written (NFR-08).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-015">SCOPE = all logs and Decision Record text written here. Identifiers only; the reject `reason` is stored on the Decision Record but never logged.</constraint>
    <constraint source="root-CLAUDE.md-§10">SCOPE = this task's BFF changes. Placement Justification in the PR (`.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`); publish-size delta vs a fresh master build (total ≤ 60 MB); no new package or HIGH CVE.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
