    <tool name="terminal">Publish-size measurement</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Intake/IntakeApprovalEndpoints.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Intake/IntakeApprovalAuthorizationFilter.cs</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Intake/IntakeApprovalService.cs</output>
    <output type="test">the three test files listed in relevant-files</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a run whose harness returned approval-required, the Approve stage creates exactly one Work Item owned by the request's owning team; redelivering the stage creates no second Work Item.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a team member and a run in AwaitingApproval, `approve` returns 200, writes one Decision Record (approved, actor = caller, approved version ids), sets the assigned attorney if unset, moves the run to Approved and enqueues one Return job.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A second `approve` of the same run returns 200 with the same Decision Record id, and no second Decision Record or Return job exists (FR-11 b).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given a team member and a run in AwaitingApproval, `reject` returns 200, writes one Decision Record (rejected), ends the run (not Failed) and sets the request stage to "In review".</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`claim` by a team member sets the assigned attorney; a claim when another attorney is already assigned returns 409 and changes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: no token → 401; a caller outside the owning team → 403 INTAKE_FORBIDDEN and nothing changes (FR-11 a); a membership read fault → 403, nothing changes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: unknown runId or a non-intake run → 404 INTAKE_RUN_NOT_FOUND; approve/reject of a run not in AwaitingApproval (other than the idempotent repeat) → 409 INTAKE_RUN_WRONG_STATE (FR-11 d); an unknown action → 400 INTAKE_INVALID_ACTION.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">With the intake kill switch off, the endpoint returns 503 INTAKE_DISABLED and writes nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The approved version ids recorded are the SPE versions current at approval (FR-11 c), read through `SpeFileStore`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No log line or ProblemDetails contains document text or the reject reason.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The PR states the Placement Justification and the publish-size delta (≤ 60 MB, no new HIGH CVE). Build and all tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: the stated contract plus the negative cases above; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in task notes. One seeding proof for the fail-closed check (break it, see the 403 test fail, restore).</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-11. Claim is an `action` on the same endpoint so one service owns the assigned-attorney invariant (ADR-002). If 013 chose other folder names than `Api/Intake/`, `Services/Intake/`, follow 013. Return is implemented by 021 and 043. Run `/conflict-check` before the PR.</notes>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
    <protocol>Before starting, load all files listed in &lt;knowledge&gt;&lt;files&gt;. Follow task-execute (FULL rigor; two adversarial-verifier passes because of the auth tag).</protocol>
  </execution>
</task>
